  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hitesh Ramesh Dama @ Nikki And Ors vs State Of Maharashtra on 21 February, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik Darshan Patil 922-aba-522-23.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 522 Of 2023 1) Hitesh Ramesh Dama @ Nikki 2) Imran Mushtak Mansuri 3) Sushil Kumar Kharwar Urf Dhiraj Kumar ..Applicants Vs. The State of Maharashtra ..Respondent ------------ Mr. Vivek Punjabi for the Applicants. Ms. A. A. Takalkar, App for the State. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J. Date : February 21, 2023 P.C. :",
    "facts": "This is an application for pre-arrest bail by the applicant in connection with First Information Report (FIR) No.I-6 of 2023 dated 04/01/2023, registered with Shanti Nagar Police Station, Thane, under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 and 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and sections 59, 30(2)(a), 26(2)(iv), 23 and 27 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 3. Applicant no. 2 is alleged to be the owner of the truck which was seized with the contraband pan masala. In the order of the Sessions Court, applicant no. 1 is also shown to Darshan Patil 922-aba-522-23.odt be the owner of the truck. Applicant no. 3 is named by the co-accused. Learned APP seeks some time to take instructions as the Investigating Officer is not present today. 4. The issue as to the interpretation of section 328 in its relation to contraband pan masala is pending before Hon'ble Supreme Court. The truck and the contraband have already been seized. The co-accused who was arrested has been granted bail. The Hitesh Ramesh Dama @ Nikki And Ors vs State Of Maharashtra on 21 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/125641907/ 1 applicants were not named in the First Information Report.",
